  "body": "The native die post in #2969 selects one through-opening in a modeled plate. The grouped post in #2974 uses two separate punch models. Permit two selected through-openings in the same retained plate with one 20 mm stock.\n\nMatch each selected rim to a different through-opening. Account for the complete plate and all of its boundaries. Each lead and each released slug needs its own clearance and holding check. Refuse duplicate rim selections, blind holes and unsafe threading or travel before writing the bundle.\n\nAn independent synthetic controller job plotted the two openings. It made the main cut for each opening, separated each slug, then ran the trim cuts. Verify a fresh CAMCraft job against that sequence and check the compensation on both rims. The control must make no cutting move through the retained plate between the openings.\n\nSuggested labels are P6, effort:high, area:post, enhancement and source:agent.\n",
